cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite the paper below."
title: "From BM25 to Corrective RAG: Benchmarking Retrieval Strategies for Text-and-Table Documents"
abstract: >-
  Benchmark code for a systematic comparison of ten retrieval strategies —
  sparse, dense, hybrid fusion, cross-encoder reranking, query expansion, index
  augmentation and adaptive retrieval — on T2-RAGBench, comprising 23,088
  financial QA queries over 7,318 documents with mixed text-and-table content.
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/mftnakrsu/rag-research-paper"
keywords:
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - hybrid retrieval
  - cross-encoder reranking
  - financial question answering
  - text-and-table documents
